  "headline": "Bareskrim Polri Assists NTT Police In Kupang Regent Rape Case",
  "seoTitle": "Kupang Regent Yosef Lede Rape Case Investigation",
  "metaDescription": "Police are advancing the investigation into sexual assault allegations against Kupang Regent Yosef Lede, denying reports that the case reached a settlement.",
  "aiSummaryBullets": [
    "The investigation into Kupang Regent Yosef Lede has been upgraded to a formal inquiry following allegations of sexual assault against a student.",
    "National Police headquarters are providing assistance to NTT regional police to support the ongoing probe into the incident.",
    "Authorities have confiscated physical evidence and interrogated 13 witnesses, explicitly dismissing claims that the case has been settled."
  ],
  "aiContextParagraph": "The East Nusa Tenggara (NTT) regional police are currently investigating allegations of sexual assault involving the Regent of Kupang, Yosef Lede. The case, which allegedly occurred at the official residence of the regent, has recently transitioned into a formal investigation phase. Police officials confirmed they have seized specific personal items as evidence and have already questioned 13 witnesses, including the individual who transported the victim to the regent's residence. Addressing public speculation, national police spokesperson Brigadier General Nurul Azizah stated that the investigation remains active and dismissed rumors suggesting the matter had been resolved through a peaceful settlement. The case has also drawn attention from high-level officials, including Vice Minister Veronica Tan, who issued a strong response regarding the seriousness of the allegations. The Bareskrim Polri is now actively assisting the NTT police to ensure a thorough investigation.",
